-- Schema 5 -> 6: the owner's phone number on the local profile row.
--
-- The number is what the account is; it is the only thing that identifies an owner to a
-- human being, and support, the paywall and WhatsApp reminders all need to find somebody by
-- it. It was never on the device at all: the server filled `profiles.phone` from a trigger
-- that runs on INSERT into auth.users, so anyone whose row was created before GoTrue set the
-- phone got NULL and nothing has ever written it since. The client could not fix that
-- because it had no column to push from.
--
-- Appended, not inserted in the middle, because ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN can only append and
-- `SELECT *` has to produce the same column order on a fresh install as on an upgraded one.
-- Profile.sq declares it last for that reason.
--
-- A plain ADD COLUMN with no NOT NULL and no default, so there is no SQLite 3.18 table
-- rebuild here. Existing rows read as NULL until the next sign-in fills them in — which is
-- correct, since the number is only known once a session proves it.
ALTER TABLE profiles ADD COLUMN phone TEXT;
